 "structure": "California History-Social Science Framework (2016) pages 692-806 of the range: Appendix C reproduces the 1998 History-Social Science Content Standards. Sections: K-5 Historical and Social Sciences Analysis Skills (Chronological and Spatial Thinking; Research, Evidence, and Point of View; Historical Interpretation); then per-grade blocks 'KINDERGARTEN', 'GRADE ONE' ... 'GRADE EIGHT', each with a title/theme, an overview paragraph, and numbered standards 'G.n Students ...' with numbered sub-standards '1.', '2.' beneath (code form grade.standard.item, e.g. 5.3 and item 4 = 5.3.4). 6-8 and 9-12 analysis-skills blocks precede grades 6 and 9-12. Grades 9-12 content: Grade Ten World History, Culture, and Geography: The Modern World (10.1-10.11), Grade Eleven United States History and Geography: Continuity and Change in the Twentieth Century (11.1-11.11), Grade Twelve Principles of American Democracy (12.1-12.10) and Principles of Economics (12.1-12.6). Page header 'History-Social Science Content Standards' and page footers 'California History-Social Science Framework | Appendix C' appear as units. Followed by non-standards appendices: D Teaching the Contemporary World (essay on four themes + suggested readings), E Educating for Democracy (civic education), F Religion and History-Social Science Education (guidelines and legal text), G California Education and the Environment Initiative (Environmental Principles and Concepts; the part of G with grade-by-grade curriculum units lies after u8058). Blank pages 'This page is intentionally left blank.' occur between appendices.",
